1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,471
Monday morning. The app is down, and the error says: cannot connect to the database.

2
00:00:06,021 --> 00:00:07,466
Is the database broken?

3
00:00:07,466 --> 00:00:08,283
Almost never.

4
00:00:08,283 --> 00:00:09,352
Most of the time,

5
00:00:09,352 --> 00:00:11,049
one small setting is wrong,

6
00:00:11,049 --> 00:00:14,191
and the error message tells you exactly which one.

7
00:00:14,741 --> 00:00:18,558
Today a real shop app cannot reach its post gress database.

8
00:00:18,558 --> 00:00:20,175
We fix it layer by layer,

9
00:00:20,175 --> 00:00:22,763
then fix a migration that fails halfway.

10
00:00:23,313 --> 00:00:26,513
Study the exact error. Change one thing. Test again.

11
00:00:28,063 --> 00:00:31,135
Here is what to expect, from the first minute to the last.

12
00:00:31,685 --> 00:00:36,549
One: the layers between an app and its database, and the error each layer produces.

13
00:00:37,099 --> 00:00:38,218
Two: a live demo.

14
00:00:38,218 --> 00:00:40,457
The app fails four times in a row,

15
00:00:40,457 --> 00:00:43,222
and we fix one setting after each failure.

16
00:00:43,772 --> 00:00:48,913
Three: a migration that fails, why it rolled back safely, and how to fix and rerun it.

17
00:00:49,463 --> 00:00:53,026
Four: your turn, with a lab that judges you with five checks.

18
00:00:53,576 --> 00:00:58,930
This is lesson eight of the databases domain, the last lesson before the mastery lesson.

19
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:02,680
Study the exact error. Change one thing. Test again.

20
00:01:04,730 --> 00:01:06,842
Eight ideas for a connection that fails.

21
00:01:07,392 --> 00:01:08,851
A connection has layers,

22
00:01:08,851 --> 00:01:10,857
and each one can fail on its own.

23
00:01:10,857 --> 00:01:11,222
First,

24
00:01:11,222 --> 00:01:14,261
the name: does the host name turn into an address?

25
00:01:14,811 --> 00:01:19,846
Second, the port: is anything listening there? A wrong port gives connection refused.

26
00:01:20,396 --> 00:01:20,770
Third,

27
00:01:20,770 --> 00:01:22,391
the login: the right user,

28
00:01:22,391 --> 00:01:23,826
and the right password.

29
00:01:23,826 --> 00:01:26,881
A wrong one gives password authentication failed.

30
00:01:27,431 --> 00:01:31,975
Fourth, the database name. A typo gives, database does not exist.

31
00:01:32,525 --> 00:01:37,816
A fifth layer is permission: the user may exist, but may not be allowed to use that table.

32
00:01:38,366 --> 00:01:41,727
A migration is a change to the database structure,

33
00:01:41,727 --> 00:01:42,870
written as S Q L.

34
00:01:42,870 --> 00:01:44,416
If one statement fails,

35
00:01:44,416 --> 00:01:47,441
a good runner rolls the whole migration back,

36
00:01:47,441 --> 00:01:49,054
so nothing is half done.

37
00:01:49,604 --> 00:01:54,959
Fix the pending migration, and rerun. Never edit a migration that is already applied.

38
00:01:55,509 --> 00:02:00,266
The method never changes: look at the exact error, change one thing, test again.

39
00:02:01,816 --> 00:02:07,512
Go to the app folder.

40
00:02:09,062 --> 00:02:10,961
Look around.

41
00:02:11,511 --> 00:02:15,415
The app's settings file, two small scripts, and a folder of migrations.

42
00:02:15,965 --> 00:02:19,527
What does the app use?

43
00:02:20,077 --> 00:02:20,554
A host,

44
00:02:20,554 --> 00:02:21,031
a port,

45
00:02:21,031 --> 00:02:22,121
a database name,

46
00:02:22,121 --> 00:02:22,598
a user,

47
00:02:22,598 --> 00:02:23,620
and a password.

48
00:02:23,620 --> 00:02:24,438
Five values,

49
00:02:24,438 --> 00:02:26,413
and any of them can be wrong.

50
00:02:26,963 --> 00:02:33,321
Start the app.

51
00:02:33,871 --> 00:02:34,311
Failed.

52
00:02:34,311 --> 00:02:38,276
Look at the error: could not translate host name D B dash shop.

53
00:02:38,276 --> 00:02:39,786
This is the first layer,

54
00:02:39,786 --> 00:02:40,353
the name.

55
00:02:40,353 --> 00:02:42,681
The computer does not know this host.

56
00:02:43,231 --> 00:02:50,037
Ask the system.

57
00:02:50,587 --> 00:02:51,550
Nothing found.

58
00:02:51,550 --> 00:02:52,995
So the name is wrong.

59
00:02:52,995 --> 00:02:56,297
The post gress server runs on this same machine,

60
00:02:56,297 --> 00:02:59,461
at one twenty-seven dot zero dot zero dot one.

61
00:03:00,011 --> 00:03:07,350
Fix the host.

62
00:03:07,900 --> 00:03:12,529
Start the app again.

63
00:03:13,079 --> 00:03:13,862
A new error.

64
00:03:13,862 --> 00:03:14,449
Progress.

65
00:03:14,449 --> 00:03:15,688
Connection refused,

66
00:03:15,688 --> 00:03:17,449
port fifty-four thirty-one.

67
00:03:17,449 --> 00:03:18,493
The name worked,

68
00:03:18,493 --> 00:03:20,058
so now the second layer,

69
00:03:20,058 --> 00:03:20,645
the port,

70
00:03:20,645 --> 00:03:21,037
fails.

71
00:03:21,587 --> 00:03:31,101
Is anything listening?

72
00:03:31,651 --> 00:03:34,318
No response. Nothing listens on that port.

73
00:03:34,868 --> 00:03:42,164
Try the real port.

74
00:03:42,714 --> 00:03:45,167
Accepting connections. That is our server.

75
00:03:45,717 --> 00:03:52,523
Fix the port.

76
00:03:53,073 --> 00:03:57,702
Start the app again.

77
00:03:58,252 --> 00:03:59,246
Progress again.

78
00:03:59,246 --> 00:04:00,769
Now the server answers,

79
00:04:00,769 --> 00:04:03,485
and says: password authentication failed.

80
00:04:03,485 --> 00:04:04,544
The third layer,

81
00:04:04,544 --> 00:04:05,207
the login.

82
00:04:05,757 --> 00:04:17,063
Where is the secret?

83
00:04:17,613 --> 00:04:22,392
The password starts with a capital S. Ours started with a small s. One letter.

84
00:04:22,942 --> 00:04:30,195
Fix the password.

85
00:04:30,745 --> 00:04:35,375
Start the app again.

86
00:04:35,925 --> 00:04:37,319
The login works now.

87
00:04:37,319 --> 00:04:40,596
The next error: database shop P does not exist.

88
00:04:40,596 --> 00:04:41,781
The fourth layer.

89
00:04:41,781 --> 00:04:43,733
A typo in the database name.

90
00:04:44,283 --> 00:04:53,819
List the databases.

91
00:04:54,369 --> 00:04:59,126
Post gress, the template databases, and shop. Our name had one extra letter.

92
00:04:59,676 --> 00:05:05,223
Fix the database name.

93
00:05:05,773 --> 00:05:10,402
Start the app again.

94
00:05:10,952 --> 00:05:11,467
App OK,

95
00:05:11,467 --> 00:05:12,275
six orders.

96
00:05:12,275 --> 00:05:13,157
Four errors,

97
00:05:13,157 --> 00:05:14,039
four layers,

98
00:05:14,039 --> 00:05:15,289
four small fixes.

99
00:05:15,289 --> 00:05:16,024
Each time,

100
00:05:16,024 --> 00:05:16,833
one change,

101
00:05:16,833 --> 00:05:17,715
then a test.

102
00:05:18,265 --> 00:05:22,489
Run the migrations.

103
00:05:23,039 --> 00:05:26,286
Zero zero one and zero zero two are skipped,

104
00:05:26,286 --> 00:05:28,131
they were applied before.

105
00:05:28,131 --> 00:05:29,828
Zero zero three failed,

106
00:05:29,828 --> 00:05:31,452
and says: rolled back,

107
00:05:31,452 --> 00:05:32,707
nothing recorded.

108
00:05:32,707 --> 00:05:36,175
The error: column status status does not exist.

109
00:05:36,175 --> 00:05:36,692
A typo.

110
00:05:37,242 --> 00:05:46,117
Look at the file.

111
00:05:46,667 --> 00:05:48,417
The second line says status,

112
00:05:48,417 --> 00:05:50,293
with two S letters at the end,

113
00:05:50,293 --> 00:05:51,106
in the index.

114
00:05:51,106 --> 00:05:53,420
The first line just added the column.

115
00:05:53,420 --> 00:05:55,546
Because it ran in one transaction,

116
00:05:55,546 --> 00:05:57,547
that column was rolled back too.

117
00:05:58,097 --> 00:06:06,182
Fix the typo.

118
00:06:06,732 --> 00:06:11,127
Run it again.

119
00:06:11,677 --> 00:06:15,261
Zero zero three is applied. Migrations up to date.

120
00:06:15,811 --> 00:06:21,741
Run it once more.

121
00:06:22,291 --> 00:06:25,619
Everything is skipped. A good runner is safe to run again.

122
00:06:26,169 --> 00:06:28,537
Run the judge.

123
00:06:29,087 --> 00:06:35,082
Five checks. Host and port, login, database, the app, and the migration. Five out of five.

124
00:06:35,632 --> 00:06:37,595
Clean up.

125
00:06:38,145 --> 00:06:40,811
The server is stopped and everything is removed.

126
00:06:41,361 --> 00:06:50,236
Is it gone?

127
00:06:50,786 --> 00:06:53,303
No response. Nothing is left behind.

128
00:06:54,853 --> 00:06:59,632
Your task. The shop app cannot start. Fix it, one layer at a time, and prove it.

129
00:07:00,182 --> 00:07:01,533
One: run check app,

130
00:07:01,533 --> 00:07:03,097
and fix the host name,

131
00:07:03,097 --> 00:07:04,093
then the port,

132
00:07:04,093 --> 00:07:05,159
in app dot env.

133
00:07:05,159 --> 00:07:06,795
Test after each change.

134
00:07:07,345 --> 00:07:12,358
Two: find the right password in the vault file, and fix it. Then fix the database name.

135
00:07:12,908 --> 00:07:14,833
Three: run migrate dot S H.

136
00:07:14,833 --> 00:07:15,474
It fails.

137
00:07:15,474 --> 00:07:18,182
Fix the typo in the pending migration,

138
00:07:18,182 --> 00:07:19,394
and run it again.

139
00:07:19,944 --> 00:07:22,013
Four: lab check, then lab down.

140
00:07:24,063 --> 00:07:27,839
Here is where to find everything. Pause on this screen, and write it down.

141
00:07:28,389 --> 00:07:30,037
The lab lives on GitHub,

142
00:07:30,037 --> 00:07:31,204
at it dash waves,

143
00:07:31,204 --> 00:07:32,784
slash dev ops dash A I,

144
00:07:32,784 --> 00:07:34,294
in the folder academy,

145
00:07:34,294 --> 00:07:34,981
slash lab.

146
00:07:35,531 --> 00:07:41,163
Two files: lab one thirty-three dot S H, and shortcuts one thirty-three dot S H.

147
00:07:41,713 --> 00:07:42,609
Install it,

148
00:07:42,609 --> 00:07:45,459
on any Linux machine: sudo install,

149
00:07:45,459 --> 00:07:47,332
dash m seven five five,

150
00:07:47,332 --> 00:07:49,694
lab one thirty-three dot S H,

151
00:07:49,694 --> 00:07:50,916
into slash usr,

152
00:07:50,916 --> 00:07:51,893
slash local,

153
00:07:51,893 --> 00:07:52,870
slash S bin.

154
00:07:53,420 --> 00:07:58,473
Load the short names with: source shortcuts one thirty-three dot S H.

155
00:07:58,473 --> 00:07:59,865
You get three: lab,

156
00:07:59,865 --> 00:08:00,158
P G,

157
00:08:00,158 --> 00:08:01,036
and use D B.

158
00:08:01,586 --> 00:08:03,218
You need post gress Q L,

159
00:08:03,218 --> 00:08:04,441
server and client,

160
00:08:04,441 --> 00:08:06,753
and port fifty-five thirteen free.

161
00:08:06,753 --> 00:08:09,472
The lab runs its own private post gress,

162
00:08:09,472 --> 00:08:10,696
in its own folder.

163
00:08:11,246 --> 00:08:13,218
Lab up prepares the broken app.

164
00:08:13,218 --> 00:08:14,936
Lab check judges your work.

165
00:08:14,936 --> 00:08:16,463
Lab down removes it all.

166
00:08:16,463 --> 00:08:18,499
Only run it on your own machine.

167
00:08:20,549 --> 00:08:22,618
Pass or fail. You need all five.

168
00:08:23,168 --> 00:08:25,408
One: the host and port reach the server.

169
00:08:25,958 --> 00:08:28,326
Two: the user and password are accepted.

170
00:08:28,876 --> 00:08:31,052
Three: the database name exists.

171
00:08:31,602 --> 00:08:34,418
Four: the app starts, and finds its six orders.

172
00:08:34,968 --> 00:08:38,040
Five: migration zero zero three is applied.

173
00:08:38,590 --> 00:08:39,892
To pass, all five.

174
00:08:41,942 --> 00:08:43,713
Your turn, on your own machine.

175
00:08:44,263 --> 00:08:47,356
One: lab up, go to the app folder, and run check app.

176
00:08:47,906 --> 00:08:50,914
Two: fix the host, then the port. Test after each.

177
00:08:51,464 --> 00:08:55,261
Three: fix the password from the vault file, then the database name.

178
00:08:55,811 --> 00:08:59,054
Four: run migrate, fix the typo, and run it again.

179
00:08:59,604 --> 00:09:03,423
Five: lab check until you see five out of five. Then lab down.

180
00:09:03,973 --> 00:09:05,807
Pause the video, and begin now.

181
00:09:21,357 --> 00:09:22,232
Quick check.

182
00:09:22,782 --> 00:09:25,832
Name the four layers where a connection can fail, in order.

183
00:09:26,382 --> 00:09:28,942
Which error means nothing is listening on the port?

184
00:09:29,492 --> 00:09:32,266
Why did the failed migration leave nothing behind?

185
00:09:32,816 --> 00:09:35,930
Why fix the pending migration, and never an applied one?

186
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:38,778
Objectives covered: M C fourteen,

187
00:09:38,778 --> 00:09:39,891
objective eight.

188
00:09:39,891 --> 00:09:44,416
Troubleshoot app to database connectivity and migration failures.

189
00:09:44,966 --> 00:09:47,036
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

190
00:09:57,586 --> 00:10:01,831
Next: the databases mastery lesson, where you prove everything together.

191
00:10:02,381 --> 00:10:05,709
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
